# Zensim stacking benchmark
# Date: 2026-03-07
# Commit: 3ffa136
# Command: /tmp/zensim_compare.sh (5 modes × 6 CLIC 1024 images × 3 distances)
# Metrics: Rust butteraugli + SSIMULACRA2 via jxl-oxide decode
#
# Modes tested:
#   e7       = effort 7, no iterative loop (baseline)
#   e8-bfly  = effort 8, butteraugli loop (2 iters)
#   e7-zen2  = effort 7, zensim loop (2 iters, no butteraugli)
#   e8-zen2  = effort 8, butteraugli loop (2 iters) + zensim loop (2 iters)
#   e8-zen4  = effort 8, butteraugli loop (2 iters) + zensim loop (4 iters)
#
# Grand average deltas vs e7 baseline:
#   e8-bfly:  size -2.6%  bfly -6.9%  ss2 -0.05
#   e7-zen2:  size +7.0%  bfly -4.0%  ss2 +1.63
#   e8-zen2:  size -0.6%  bfly -5.3%  ss2 +0.42
#   e8-zen4:  size +0.3%  bfly -0.1%  ss2 +0.66
#
# Conclusion: butteraugli loop alone gives best RD efficiency.
# Zensim most useful at e7 for SSIM2 improvement.
